# Allowlisted production package-level mutable variables in backend/.
#
# archcheck (tools/quality/archcheck) flags any package-level var that is not
# an error sentinel, compile-time assertion, embed.FS value, basic/byte-string
# literal. Composite literals are mutable and must be listed here when an
# intentional package-owned lookup table cannot be a constant. Only genuinely
# process-global-by-design values belong here; new entries require a documented
# justification (see the mutable-globals rule in main.go).
#
# Format: <relative-path>:<varName>, one per line.
#
# The middleware rate-limiter singleton is a mutex-protected process-global
# rate-limiting instance (not an application dependency); its test hooks are
# gated to APP_ENV=test. Documented in docs/agent-engineering.md (Dependency
# direction and ownership).
backend/internal/middleware/rate_limit.go:limiter

# Static lookup tables. Go has no constant arrays/slices; both remain private
# to their owning packages and are never exposed or mutated after startup.
backend/internal/progression/ranks.go:rankDefinitions
backend/internal/validation/upload_validator.go:allowedImageTypes
